LLM Code Self-Assessment — Prabhleen Kaur

Sprint: Sprint 2, 3–17 September 2026
Code assessed: Frontend and Homepage
Branch: Frontend / Homepage

What I built

During this sprint, I mainly worked on the frontend and homepage of our project. My task was to create the homepage structure and make sure the important information is easy for users to find. I worked with React components and connected different parts of the homepage together. I also focused on keeping the layout simple and user-friendly.

What I agree with

The LLM suggested that the homepage should be divided into reusable components instead of putting everything inside one large component. I agree with this because smaller components make the code easier to understand, update, and reuse.

It also pointed out that naming should stay clear and consistent. This is important when working in a team because other members should easily understand what each component does.

What I do not agree with

The LLM suggested adding more advanced optimisation to the frontend. I do not think this is necessary at this stage because our project is still small. My main focus was making the homepage work correctly and match our project requirements.

What I would do differently

If I did this again, I would plan the homepage components more clearly before starting the code. I would also test the page on different screen sizes earlier so that responsive design is easier to manage.

What I learned

I learned more about React components, homepage structure, and organising frontend code. I also improved my Git and GitHub skills during the sprint. Working with my team helped me improve my communication and teamwork skills, and I became more confident in explaining my own code.
